# HARDENING-EXCEPTIONS — role units that do not carry a baseline sandbox
# directive, checked by scripts/ci/lint-systemd-hardening.sh.
#
# An UNDECLARED gap fails the lint, and so does a declared one the unit no
# longer has; closing an entry means hardening the unit, then deleting the
# line. Not a template: nothing in the role renders or copies this file.
#
# Format: <unit>:<directive>  # why

# lock-path is the default /tmp/pgbackrest, shared with archive-push,
# manual backups and `pgbackrest stop`; see the unit's own comment.
pgbackrest-backup.service:PrivateTmp

# Run as root and drop to postgres with `sudo -u`; no-new-privs blocks
# sudo's setuid transition (BDR-04, see the units' own comments).
restore-drill.service:NoNewPrivileges
restore-drill-offsite.service:NoNewPrivileges

# Pre-existing and not yet reviewed: runs as root under run-heavy-job.sh
# (its comment explains the root, not the missing no-new-privs).
asset-registry-backfill.service:NoNewPrivileges

# Pre-existing and not yet reviewed: these run as root for root's mc
# aliases (~/.mc/config.json), which rules out ProtectHome, but nothing
# records why the rest of the baseline is absent.
galexie-archive-contiguity.service:NoNewPrivileges
galexie-archive-contiguity.service:PrivateTmp
galexie-archive-contiguity.service:ProtectKernelTunables
